Commodore 128 for MEGA65 aka c128Mega65
=======================================

done in 2024-2026 by
    * Stefan Eilers   github.com/eilers
    * Jeff Flitton    github.com/jflitton

c128Mega65 is licensed under the terms of GNU/GPL v3, for more information
please read the file LICENSE. Parts of c128Mega65 are licensed under other
Free-software licenses as described in the source code.

c128Mega65:
-----------

  c128Mega65 is a port of MiSTer's C128_MiSTer
      done by Erik Scheffers (eriks5)
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/C128_MiSTer

  C128_MiSTer is based on MiSTer's C64_MiSTer
      done by the MiSTer Development Team
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/C64_MiSTer
      Significant contributors:
      * sorgelig
      * vpelletier
      * raparici

  MiSTer's C64_MiSTer is a port of MiST's C64 core
      done by the MiST Development Team
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/mist-devel/c64
      Significant contributors:
      * gyurco
      * nippur72
      * harbaum

  MiST's C64 core is a port of FPGA64_027 and 1541_SD
      done by Dar (darfpga@aol.fr)
      http://darfpga.blogspot.fr

  FPGA64_027 and 1541_SD is a port of FPGA64
      done by Peter Wendrich
      https://www.syntiac.com/fpga64.html

  The 8502 CPU is based on T65
      done by Daniel Wallner, Mike Johnson, Wolfgang Scherr, Morten Leikvoll

  The Z80 CPU is based on T80
      done by Daniel Wallner

Other than that and our own work, c128Mega65 uses:
--------------------------------------------------

  * MiSTer2MEGA65 by The MiSTer2MEGA65 Development Team, including its Shell
    (the on-screen menu), which we ported from QNICE to RISC-V
    https://github.com/sy2002/MiSTer2MEGA65

  * Parts of C64MEGA65 by MJoergen and sy2002: the virtual cartridge (.crt)
    support, the internal 3.5" floppy drive (physical_1581), the SDRAM
    controller and the Ethernet MAC
    https://github.com/MJoergen/C64MEGA65

  * NEORV32 RISC-V processor by Stephan Nolting, for the system CPU and the
    SwiftLink modem
    https://github.com/stnolting/neorv32

  * FatFs file system module by ChaN
    http://elm-chan.org/fsw/ff/

  * lwIP TCP/IP stack by Adam Dunkels and the lwIP team
    https://savannah.nongnu.org/projects/lwip/

  * SD card host controller (sdhost) from Megamiga by Johan Smolinski
    https://github.com/johansmolinski/Megamiga

  * CCGMS Future terminal by Craig Smith, alwyz and Michael Steil, used to
    test the SwiftLink modem
    https://github.com/mist64/ccgmsterm

  * Various MEGA65 drivers taken from the MEGA65 VHDL source by Paul Gardner-Stephen
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-core

  * VGA Timing Generator, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=15925278

  * VGA to HDMI converter IP core, done by Adam Barnes
    https://github.com/amb5l/tyto2

  * AVALON SCALER used for scaling to 720p for HDMI, done by temlib.org
    http://temlib.org/site/?page_id=10

  * HyperRAM controller, done by MJoergen
    https://mjoergen.github.io/HyperRAM/

  * Debouncer: I/O debouncing used for the joysticks, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=4980758

  * Anikki-16x16 font, archived and provided by k80w
    https://github.com/k80w/consolefonts

  * PSF font to text file converter nafe-0.1 by Corvus Corax
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/nafe/

  * PSF font to C include file converter psftools-1.1.1 by John Elliott
    https://www.seasip.info/Unix/PSF/

The following resources were invaluable for developing c128Mega65:
------------------------------------------------------------------

  * 1541 Ultimate by Gideon Zweijtzer: the SwiftLink's 6551 ACIA follows its
    acia6551, which was measured on a real 6551
    https://github.com/GideonZ/1541ultimate
